config PHYSICAL_ANTI_FRAGMENTATION
	bool "Physical memory anti-fragmentation"
	depends on !S390
	default y
	help
	  Split the buddy allocator free lists of each zone into four
	  free areas (FLCs) covering equal page frame ranges, and keep
	  the pages of every free list ordered by their physical
	  address.

	  Free pages are inserted into the area matching their PFN and
	  are kept sorted around the midpoint of that area.  For order
	  3 and above the free area index is mirrored, so allocation
	  preference runs from the opposite end of the zone.  This
	  keeps large contiguous blocks together and reduces physical
	  memory fragmentation on long-running devices.

	  Say Y here to enable physical memory anti-fragmentation.
	  If unsure, say Y.
